- If describing all panels/elements will clearly exceed 700 characters → MUST be COMPLEX

Classify this image as **SIMPLE**, **MODERATE**, or **COMPLEX** based on these criteria:

### SIMPLE:
Classify as SIMPLE if the image meets ALL of the following criteria:
    - MANDATORY: Exactly one panel only (no sub-figures, insets, side-by-side comparisons, or multiple views).
    - MANDATORY: 8 or fewer distinct text labels total (including axis titles, legend keys, callouts, annotations).
    - MANDATORY: No more than 2 data series OR 2 discrete visual objects (e.g., single line graph, single bar chart, one or two simple objects).
    - MANDATORY: No stacked/layered visuals (no pyramids, heatmaps, overlays, funnels, composite images).
    - MANDATORY: No complex microscopy, multi-view radiology, or anatomical cut-aways requiring extensive description.
    - MANDATORY: Uses flat color or grayscale (4 or fewer total colors); no complex gradients or heatmaps.
    - MANDATORY: No logarithmic or dual y-axes, no secondary axis grids.
    - MANDATORY: No complex math equations, multiple Greek letters, or chemical structure diagrams.
    - MANDATORY: No rotation or 3D/perspective distortion (image should be 2D, head-on).
    - MANDATORY: No error bars, confidence intervals, or complex statistical annotations.
    - Caption is 25 words or fewer.
    - Single focused scene or straightforward visualization.
    - Clear main subject that can be described briefly and completely.
    - The core message can be conveyed in under 230 characters (including prefix and suffix).
    
    DISQUALIFIERS FOR SIMPLE - If ANY of these are present, classify as MODERATE or COMPLEX:
    - Multiple panels or sub-figures
    - More than 2 data series or lines on a graph
    - Multiple comparisons across groups or time points
    - Complex medical imaging requiring detailed anatomical description
    - More than 8 labels or annotations
    - Dense data visualization (scatter plots with many points, heatmaps, forest plots)
    - Requires extensive technical explanation
    - Multiple interconnected elements or processes
    
    EXAMPLES OF SIMPLE IMAGES:
    - A single line graph with one or two lines and basic axis labels
    - A basic bar chart with 2-4 bars
    - A single clinical photograph showing one clear finding
    - A simple diagram with minimal labels
    - A single X-ray or scan showing one straightforward feature
    
    SIMPLE images should represent approximately 10-20% of scientific/medical images - those that are genuinely straightforward and require minimal description.

### MODERATE: 
Classify as MODERATE if the image has the following characteristics:
    - 2-3 panels or sub-figures requiring comparison
    - 2-4 data series or visual objects requiring comparison
    - Moderate labeling (9-15 text labels)
    - Single graph with 2-4 lines/bars requiring trend analysis
    - Medical/scientific images with moderate complexity (2-3 anatomical features, comparative views)
    - Requires structured description with multiple sentences
    - Some specialized terminology requiring explanation
    - Moderate information density
    - Caption between 25-50 words
    - Requires domain knowledge but not highly specialized
    - Description length between 230-700 characters
    - Can be adequately described in a single paragraph under 700 characters
    
    MODERATE represents standard scientific/medical images with moderate complexity that don't require extensive multi-paragraph descriptions.

### COMPLEX: 
Classify as COMPLEX if the image has ANY of the following characteristics:
    - 4 or more panels or sub-figures (AUTOMATIC COMPLEX)
    - 5 or more data series requiring detailed comparison (AUTOMATIC COMPLEX)
    - Multiple overlapping layers of information requiring sequential explanation
    - Dense data visualization (heatmaps with multiple variables, multi-series scatter plots, forest plots with many comparisons)
